  "question": {
    "text": "The mean of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> distinct observations is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;and their variance is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>.</mo></math> If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> out of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> observations are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then the remaining two observations are:",
